    summary: "Eilean Therapeutics Inc. is a privately held small-molecule oncology company established in 2022, according to the company, focused on pan-variant therapies for haematological malignancies. Its pipeline lists lomonitinib (FLT3/IRAK4, acute myeloid leukaemia), lonitoclax (BCL2), balomenib (menin) and ZE74-0282, a selective inhibitor of mutated JAK2 V617F for polycythaemia vera and myelofibrosis, together with preclinical programmes. Its only registry study sponsored under this name, through the Australian subsidiary Eilean Therapeutics AU Pty Ltd, is a phase 1 safety study of ZE74-0282 in healthy volunteers (NCT07527221), posted on ClinicalTrials.gov in April 2026; it has no registered cancer trial under this sponsor name.",
